.TITLE "lsblk"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Lists information about all available or specified block devices. It is the best way to see a __visual tree__ of your hard drives, partitions, and mount points.

.DIV "TLDR"
**lsblk**
Displays a list of all block devices in a tree-like format.
> 

**lsblk -f**
Includes information about the filesystem type and labels for each partition.
> __-f__ filesystem flag

**lsblk -m**
Displays information about the permissions and ownership of the devices.
> __-m__ permissions flag

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Using __lsblk__ is much safer than __fdisk__ for simply viewing your storage layout, as it does not require root privileges and cannot accidentally modify your partitions. It is a great tool for identifying which device corresponds to a specific drive.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:df** **linux:mount** **linux:free**

